  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Three actually inspected2015/2021 front and west-transept photographs plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. No bespoke plans/surveys researched or pictures redistributed. Hidden rear/roof details,all heights and exact host terrain joins remain approximate/unverified.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monaco_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame-de-l%27Immacul%C3%A9e-Concepcion_Ext%C3%A9rieure_Facade_1.jpg",
        "author": "Zairon",
        "date": "2021-10-03",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected front/side photograph. Pale coursed limestone front has three deep round-headed porch openings and timber portals,paired slender support columns with intermediate capitals,small gabled canopy crowns and a broad stepped approach. Upper front includes two tiers of clustered round windows,a large central wheel rose above three narrow lights,blind arcade bands and a raised central relief/gable. Corner pilasters/abstract finials frame the slopes. A short rounded front corner chapel/stair has upper windows;small polygonal gray-roof turret and distant square open tower/octagonal crossing lantern are visible. Fine sculpture and hidden roof geometry unresolved."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monaco_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame-de-l%27Immacul%C3%A9e-Concepcion_Ext%C3%A9rieure_Face_Ouest_3.jpg",
        "author": "Zairon",
        "date": "2021-10-03",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected west-transept photograph. Broad projecting gabled transept has a deep round side doorway,three upper round windows with taller middle head and a lower three-window tier. A descending blind-arcade band follows the gable. Adjacent aisle has paired round lights/cornice;rear square tower has lower paired arches and four actual open small upper belfry arches under a flat projecting tiled cap. Tan adjacent civic building/statue are separate host content. Height/current hidden rear and delicate carving remain estimates."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monaco_-_panoramio_(168).jpg",
        "author": "Patrick F",
        "date": "2015-05-15",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected useful close front-oblique overview. Confirms three deep round porches and separate timber doors,slender paired two-stage supports/strong capitals,upper central rose/three lights,two rows of flanking arcaded fields,blind arcade strips,central relief/gable and small abstract roof figures. Front corner round chapel has upper round windows/flat cornice and a small gray polygonal roof behind. Broad stairs approach the doors. Surrounding trees/city and exact heraldry/figures are excluded."
      }
    ]
  }
